      },
      {
        "sha": "c85e7b6cd5f812081bbfe44fb657ce89ffebfcc3",
        "node_id": "MDY6Q29tbWl0MjAxMTMzNzYxOmM4NWU3YjZjZDVmODEyMDgxYmJmZTQ0ZmI2NTdjZTg5ZmZlYmZjYzM=",
        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "name": "Ivo List",
            "email": "ilist@google.com",
            "date": "2020-11-18T18:26:51Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "GitHub",
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "date": "2020-11-18T18:26:51Z"
          },
          "message": "Fix conditional select on darwin. (#1674)\n\nBazel is changing how @bazel_tools/conditions:darwin is implemented.\r\nWith old implementation based on flags, it was ok to have darwin and\r\ndarwin_x86_64 in a select. This was base on flag --cpu=darwin and\r\n--cpu=dawin_x86_64.\r\n\r\nNew implementation is based on constraints, where \"darwin\" means OS (and\r\nany CPU), while \"darwin_x86_64\" mean only specific CPU. As such they\r\ncannot be used in the same select, because the selection would be\r\nambiguous.",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "e7a3285c0716c36ddc605af531dd2a90de9986a6",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/rules_docker/git/trees/e7a3285c0716c36ddc605af531dd2a90de9986a6"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/rules_docker/git/commits/c85e7b6cd5f812081bbfe44fb657ce89ffebfcc3",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJftWdrCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAdHIIAKHnpbFqF++EX6YwvRXrJpvQ\nsX0VRzpO3l3a0DzKZHfqVYGTNsLWcZLUbFbzvkOXAcwgFGcFqnOis1kCmWVqcpEo\n+tQB6Nh+2RPJQagYp0fjEHtyNXqUUJ3qIlxbWb9wWE7rSKPq1stfgSOx+Sjrp2P+\nL8BAgm2UXUSOYZVK4jusm58Jqyk8dpyWG6AtvhXfKuk+3GwDOA2Sr/hluGfTNtu3\nU+t0zoNNRgT9e4qM60trJB+ffMEJyBFPakaghfM4da56V476UynCcskyw5EWT2mS\nT5hOOyPr1a8yhn3rvHRakXlvMCSmUBf2I4HaBRyh+3E3jz4ZCEVE9UAF9PTyhNc=\n=1o4R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree e7a3285c0716c36ddc605af531dd2a90de9986a6\nparent 1bdeab8ef67d47db4eeebbe77f732811fac84dcc\nauthor Ivo List <ilist@google.com> 1605724011 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1605724011 -0500\n\nFix conditional select on darwin. (#1674)\n\nBazel is changing how @bazel_tools/conditions:darwin is implemented.\r\nWith old implementation based on flags, it was ok to have darwin and\r\ndarwin_x86_64 in a select. This was base on flag --cpu=darwin and\r\n--cpu=dawin_x86_64.\r\n\r\nNew implementation is based on constraints, where \"darwin\" means OS (and\r\nany CPU), while \"darwin_x86_64\" mean only specific CPU. As such they\r\ncannot be used in the same select, because the selection would be\r\nambiguous."
          }
        },
